    {
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Known observability gaps",
      "gridPos": { "h": 1, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 54 },
      "id": 106
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "No alerting rules, no NL-bridge panel, unlabeled replica-lag gauge defaults to 0",
      "gridPos": { "h": 6, "w": 24, "x": 0, "y": 55 },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "No Prometheus alerting rule exists for any panel on this dashboard - confirmed platform-wide absence, not a Module-09-specific gap (docs/adr/0112, mirrors every sibling module's own Phase 8). `analytics_replica_lag_seconds` is an *unlabeled* Gauge that prom-client initializes to `0` the moment it registers, before the first real sample - a freshly-booted instance's panel reads `0` regardless of whether a replica is actually configured or caught up; pair this panel with `analytics_mv_refresh_job_runs_total`'s own activity before trusting a `0` reading as \"healthy\" (`MvFreshnessMonitorService`'s own doc comment). There is no panel for `askAnalyticsQuestion` (Phase 7) - every real call to it fails with `NL_QUERY_BRIDGE_UNAVAILABLE` (ADR-0111, Module 10 does not exist), so there is no successful-answer metric to show; a future panel here would need Module 10 to exist first. `EXPORT_MAX_ROWS`/`MAX_LIMIT` cost-tier thresholds were validated at this build's own small real data volume (docs/module-09-phase-8-load-test-results.md), not at their own numeric ceiling - no panel distinguishes a query that hit `MAX_LIMIT` from one that didn't, since `MetricQueryEngineService` doesn't emit that as a separate label today."
      }
    }
  ]
